  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nThe vision adapter never fired for an image that arrived **inside a tool result**, so those requests went to a model documented not to accept images, and analytics recorded an ordinary route.\n\nMeasured on the live request log (read-only):\n\n```\ntotal rows                       115,522\nroute_diversion IS NOT NULL            0\nroute_chain IS NOT NULL           71,654   (tracing live since 8 Aug)\nroute_attempt > 0                    608   (fallbacks DO get recorded)\n```\n\nThe gate was open the whole time — `/admin/api/models` reports `nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free` (the configured Sonnet primary) in `blind_models`, and `MODEL_VISION` is set.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`request_carries_image` walked only the top level of each message's content:\n\n```python\nreturn any(\n    isinstance(block, ContentBlockImage)\n    for message in request.messages\n    if isinstance(message.content, list)\n    for block in message.content\n)\n```\n\n`ContentBlockToolResult.content` is `str | list[Any] | dict`, and an image returned by a tool (reading a PNG, an MCP screenshot) is nested inside it. Probed against the real model:\n\n```\n True  top-level image block          (pasted screenshot)\nFalse  image inside a tool_result     (Read tool / MCP screenshot)\nFalse  document block                 (PDF)\n```\n\n## What this does\n\n- **Detection** — `request_image_inputs` walks tool-result content at bounded depth and counts `document` blocks too: a model that cannot read an image cannot read a PDF.\n- **Recording** — `input_image_count` on the row, plus a downscaled WebP thumbnail in its own content-addressed table. Claude Code re-sends the conversation each turn, so keying on the source bytes stores one screenshot once rather than once per turn (measured: 5 requests, 1 stored blob). Retention deletes links with their rows, and a picture once no surviving request points at it.\n- **Settings** — `REQUEST_LOG_CAPTURE_IMAGES` and `REQUEST_LOG_IMAGE_MAX_PIXELS` (0 records the image without pixels), both bounded through `config/limits.py` and on the Limits page.\n- **Dashboard** — an `image` / `N images` chip on the row, an \"Image input\" line and the thumbnails in the detail, and a \"With image input\" figure in the window stats, counted separately from the diversion because a vision-capable primary takes an image without diverting at all.\n\nThumbnailing runs at finalize time, never between the client and its first token, and never raises — an unreadable image is still recorded as an image that arrived.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Probe of the real router**: a `tool_result` image and a PDF both divert, `plan.diversion is RouteDiversion.VISION`, and the row reads back `route_diversion='vision'`.\n- **Mutation-tested guards** — each broken on purpose, each turned the suite red by name: detector stops walking tool results (3 + 1 failures), prune stops deleting orphaned images (1), per-request instead of deduped storage (6), thumbnail failure raises instead of degrading (1).\n- **Full suite**: 3858 passed, 6 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures — identical to unmodified `fork/main`.\n- **Real browser** on a throwaway home (port 8177): chips render, both thumbnails decode at 512×320 and 329×512, the PDF row shows \"no preview stored\", a text-only row hides the pane, no console errors, and the chip passes AA in all four themes (5.38–9.38:1).\n- The live WSL server on `:8082` answered 200 afterwards and was never touched.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **Existing rows cannot gain images they never stored.** The count and thumbnails start from this version.\n- **URL image sources are counted but have no pixels to keep** — the proxy does not fetch them.\n- Storage grows by one thumbnail per distinct image (tens of KB), bounded by row retention and by `REQUEST_LOG_IMAGE_MAX_PIXELS=0` for anyone who wants counts only.\n- `pillow` is a new runtime dependency, locked in `uv.lock` with the version bump.\n\nVersion 5.12.0 → **5.13.0** (MINOR: new capability).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
