    "message": "feat(analytics): record image input, and divert on images a tool delivered\n\nThe vision adapter never fired for an image that arrived inside a tool\nresult, so those requests went to a model documented not to accept images\nand analytics recorded an ordinary route. On the user's live log:\n115,522 rows, 71,654 with route tracing, and zero with route_diversion set.\n\nMechanism: request_carries_image walked only the top level of each\nmessage's content and isinstance-checked ContentBlockImage. An image\nreturned by a tool -- reading a PNG, an MCP screenshot -- is nested inside\nthat tool_result block's own content, which was never inspected. Its\ndocstring asserted \"tool results reach the model as their own blocks\",\nwhich is not true of the Anthropic schema.\n\nrequest_image_inputs now walks tool_result content (bounded depth) and\ncounts document blocks, since a model that cannot read an image cannot\nread a PDF either. Every image found is recorded: input_image_count on the\nrow, and a downscaled WebP thumbnail in its own content-addressed table so\nthe request detail can show what the model was looking at. Claude Code\nre-sends the conversation each turn, so keying on the source bytes stores\none screenshot once instead of once per turn -- measured 5 requests, 1\nstored blob. Retention deletes links with their rows and a picture once no\nsurviving request points at it.\n\nTwo bounded settings, both on the Limits page: REQUEST_LOG_CAPTURE_IMAGES\nand REQUEST_LOG_IMAGE_MAX_PIXELS (0 records the image without any pixels).\nThumbnailing happens at finalize time, never between the client and its\nfirst token, and never raises: an unreadable image is still recorded as an\nimage that arrived.\n\nDashboard: an \"image\"/\"N images\" chip on the row, an \"Image input\" line and\nthe thumbnails in the detail, and a \"With image input\" figure in the window\nstats, counted separately from the diversion because a vision-capable\nprimary takes an image without any diversion at all.\n\nVerification:\n- probe of the real router: a tool_result image and a PDF both divert,\n  plan.diversion is vision, and the row reads back route_diversion=vision\n- 5 new test files / 34 tests; four guards mutation-tested (detector stops\n  walking tool results; prune stops deleting orphans; per-request instead\n  of deduped storage; thumbnail failure raises) -- each turned the suite\n  red by name\n- full suite 3858 passed, 6 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures,\n  identical to unmodified fork/main\n- real browser on a throwaway home (port 8177): chips, both thumbnails\n  decoding at 512x320 and 329x512, the PDF row showing \"no preview stored\",\n  a text-only row hiding the pane, no console errors, and the chip passing\n  AA in all four themes (5.38-9.38:1)\n- live WSL :8082 answered 200 afterwards and was never touched\n\nNot done: existing rows cannot gain images they never stored, and\nsandbox-style URL image sources are counted but have no pixels to keep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
